## Joining this project

Already have the code repo cloned? Set up `.cursor` like this:

```bash
cd <project-name>                                                        # code repo root
git clone git@bitbucket.org:astoundcommerce/sfcc-next-cursor.git .cursor
cd .cursor && git checkout {{PROJECT_BRANCH}} && cd ..
```

Then open the `<project-name>` folder in Cursor and run:

```
/project:init
```

It detects the project is already initialized and just copies `.env.example` → `.env` for you — no
questions asked. It also clones `legacy_code/` (legacy codebase, if configured) and `base-sf-next/`
(clean Storefront Next template from `SalesforceCommerceCloud/storefront-next-template` branch
`latest`) if they are missing, so any subsequent run also acts as a repair. Finally, fill in your own
credentials in `.cursor/.project/.env`:

```
ATLASSIAN_EMAIL=your@email.com
ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN=<token>
```

Token URL: https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens

That's it — you're set up.

