## Refreshing project memory

Run the preflight sync on `{{PROJECT_BRANCH}}`:

```
/project:sync
```

`/project:sync` pulls the latest tooling on this project branch (`git -C .cursor pull --ff-only`),
force-refreshes the OpenSpec schema/config (`openspec/config.yaml` + `openspec/schemas/`) from the
library, then refreshes and reindexes project-context. Your client deliverables (`openspec/specs/`,
`openspec/changes/`) are never touched.

To adopt upstream tooling fixes onto this branch, merge `master`/`main` into `{{PROJECT_BRANCH}}`
manually at the git/GitHub level — then the next `/project:sync` fast-forwards your local checkout.

